# Источник: собственная правка проекта, утверждена пользователем (REPORT-GQAVEC2.md); gqavec1 не брать (ошибка качества).
# gqavec2.patch: GQA-packed decode path for the HIP vec flash-attention kernel (full patch, replaces gqavec1.patch)
#
# Kernel code is IDENTICAL to gqavec1.patch (GGML_HIP_FA_GQA_VEC=1, off by default; see REPORT-GQAVEC1.md for the design).
# What is new in this version (GQAVEC2): the investigation of "KL 0.02" found NO kernel bug (REPORT-GQAVEC2.md): the model amplifies
# rounding-level differences, base ub2 vs base ub1 gives the same KL (0.025). This patch adds permanent tests:
#   tests/test-backend-ops.cpp: test_flash_attn_ext_peaky (peaky K, outlier channels, masked tail, small kv incl. 256/768, nb 1/2, NMSE 1e-4,
#   env PEAKY_OUTLIER / PEAKY_MASKTAIL / PEAKY_NMSE; set PEAKY_NMSE=1e-12 to print every case's NMSE).
# Applies on top of 95d26d1 + slot-checkpoints.patch + upstream-picks.patch + reports/forktune1/forktune1.patch.
#
